feat(context): signal-driven dhikr suggestions (domain layer)

Surfaces an authentic dhikr from the local corpus when the day's context
calls for one: weather at the user's location, the Islamic calendar, and a
coarse reading of the news.

Design contract
---------------
News is a SIGNAL, never CONTENT. No headline, outlet, place, party or number
is stored or displayed. A signal only chooses which already-verified dhikr is
shown, and the dhikr speaks for itself. This keeps the guarantee in
docs/AI_SAFETY.md intact, avoids any appearance of editorialising about
contested events, and reproduces no third-party text.

The editorial line is comfort-only, and it is enforced in code: a conflict
headline is classified as actionable ONLY when it also carries a marker of
human loss, and the resulting suggestion is a supplication of patience that
names nobody. Elections, summits, markets and sport resolve to silence.
test/context_awareness_test.dart asserts this directly, so a regression that
starts the app commenting on politics fails the build.

Silence over substitution: topics whose prescribed adhkar are not yet in the
seed corpus (eclipse, earthquake, snow, Ashura) are detected but produce no
suggestion. docs/CONTEXT_CORPUS_GAPS.md lists what needs sourcing and
grading; that is scholarly work, not code.

This commit is the domain layer only - pure Dart, no plugins, no network, so
CI can verify all of it. Arabic matching is token-boundary based rather than
substring, the failure mode that previously classified اللهم as worry.

Fetching (Open-Meteo, which needs no API key, so no secret ships in the APK),
the on-device RSS reader and the home card follow once this core is green.

